reims-vgpu: publish each changed present frame into a file the viewer reads without QMP.

The desktop's live view polled `screendump` (ppm, 1179x2556, ~9 MB) about
16 times a second through the control plane (native/ios_emulator/control.rs
frame_file), changed or not. QEMU runs `screendump` as a coroutine command on
its main loop with the BQL held (ui/ui-qmp-cmds.c qmp_screendump: "coroutine-
only ... main thread only"): qemu_console_co_wait_update schedules
console_hw_update_bh -> graphic_hw_update -> reims_vgpu_mmio_fb_update (device
poll + host-action delivery) and waits for it, then ppm_save converts the
console surface row by row through pixman (qemu_pixman_linebuf_fill to
PIXMAN_BE_r8g8b8) and writes it with qio_channel_write_all on a blocking file
descriptor, which never yields. Measured: QEMU main
thread 68 % busy during swipes, the six vCPU threads ~20 %, `irq_wait` (IRQ
delivery through the main-loop BH) 0.29 ms mean with hops up to 277 ms.

The device already holds the frame: every accepted DisplaySwap on a host
whose window does not carry it converts the front surface into the retained
BGRA8 frame (`PresentState::frame_bgra`, reims-present-capture-in-place) on
the present drain. Now, when REIMS_VGPU_FRAME_MAILBOX names a file
(tools/run_ios_paravirt.py sets it for interactive sessions to
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tomacco/ios-mailbox/<token>/frames, the directory 0700
and locked by the launcher), `runtime::frame_mailbox::offer` copies that retain
into a hand-off buffer (one memcpy under the device lock, allocation reused;
a frame the writer has not taken yet is replaced by the newer one) and a
thread of its own (`reims-frame-mailbox`) compares it with the frame it
published last and, only when the bytes differ, writes it into the file:

  4 KiB header (magic PSFRMBX1, version 1, 2 slots, slot capacity, writer pid,
  newest frame number, instance) + two slots of one tight BGRA8 frame each.
  Frame n lives in slot n % 2; its slot sequence is 2n+1 while it is written
  and 2n once complete, then the header's newest number becomes n. A reader
  takes n, requires 2n before and after copying the slot and retries
  otherwise; a geometry change empties both slots and the newest number
  before it resizes the file.

The writer creates the file itself (O_CREAT|O_EXCL, 0600), refuses a
directory others may enter, an existing file and a link, and never grows the
file past the process's RLIMIT_FSIZE (read from /proc/self/limits; a write
past it would be SIGXFSZ). Every refusal and the first write failure is one
fail-log line (`frame_mailbox_refused`, `frame_mailbox_publish_failed`); the
census `OFF frame_mailbox published= unchanged= coalesced= failed= offered=
offer_us= write_us= frame=` is written at power-of-two publish counts. Without
the variable nothing here runs and nothing the guest sees changes either way:
the mailbox is fed from the retain after the present's own work.

The control plane (native/ios_emulator/control.rs mailbox_frame_file) answers
`frame` transport=file from the mailbox without opening QMP: an unchanged
frame number is `changed:false` with the existing file and touches nothing;
a new frame is converted BGRA -> PPM in tomaccoctl's process. With no mailbox
or no frame in it yet (an older engine, boot before the first present) it
falls back to screendump.

Tests: runtime::frame_mailbox::tests (round trip of number/geometry/bytes, a
slot being rewritten is never handed out, geometry change empties before it
resizes, file-limit refusal keeps the previous frame, private-directory /
existing-file / link refusals, the writer thread publishes only changed
frames and coalesces bursts, a reader racing the writer never takes a mixed
frame); reims-vgpu-config a_frame_mailbox_is_an_absolute_path_or_nothing.

